e moved for the Free State Project  libertarians are such a small part of  the population in most states that  you're never actually going to be able  to break into the two-party system and  make any change but if you found a state  with a low population like New Hampshire  there's only a million people in the  whole state plus it already has a  Liberty leaning kind of mentality anyway  live free or die that if you concentrate  a bunch of activists not just normal  people but activists in a state that you  could actually maybe see some progress  have you seen any specific progress  anything moving in the Liberty direction  twelve Free Staters have actually been  elected to office and I think that  that's pretty amazing actually fish  pedicures are still illegal there for  those who don't know that's a practice  that's pretty common in parts of Asia  were little toothless fish basically  give you a pedicure we interviewed this  Vietnamese woman who invested a bunch of  money into this practice and the state  basically shut her down it just shows  how much progress there still is yet to  be made what are some of the things that  people think about when they think of  New Hampshire you can drive your  motorcycle without a helmet no helmet  laws no seatbelt laws i think there's no  seat belt laws that could be wrong about  that there's no seat belt laws for  adults I think they actually have some  of the safest streets in America  elastomer checks they don't have sales  tax or income tax and they were the  first state to legalize civil unions  without being forced to by the judiciary  so I mean they don't have gay marriage  but they were the first state that just  passed it through the house just said  yeah this is the right thing to do and  want to head with it New Hampshire is a  great State for Liberty lovers and I  think that the more people like the Free  Staters who move in the more it will  just become the folks who are there the  Free Staters who are there how do they  regard the movement now are they  thinking that it's better than they  expected are they disappointed or is it  all over the place in terms of opinion  the standard line that I get is that  people who moved to New Hampshire don't  know why they didn't do it  everybody who moves there is actually  really happy to be there and i think is  very optimistic about the the project in  its future  you
 

